text:
elaine: Quick check — I ran terraform apply for the models overlay and now the per-model configmap mount path changed in the pod spec from /etc/flags to /app/config/flags. I didn't touch that path in TF. Plan showed a replace for k8s_deployment.models-web, anyone seen this drift?

sam: hmm, any chance kustomize overlay got swapped? we have a kustomize base that sets mountPath, and the overlay in the repo sometimes gets replaced by ci artifact.

mike: can you paste the plan diff snippet? that helps. sometimes controller rewrite when annotations change.

elaine: plan snippet:```~ resource "kubernetes_deployment" "models-web" {
  ~ spec {
      ~ template {
          ~ spec {
              ~ containers {
                  ~ volume_mount {
                      ~ mount_path = "/etc/flags" -> "/app/config/flags" # forces replace
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}```

sam: oh interesting — the mount_path change is coming from the rendered manifest rather than TF variables. search repo for /app/config/flags — maybe some new helm/kustomize overlay introduced it.

dee: infra-bot: detected configmap name collision between namespace models-staging and models-int. Recommend explicit namespace scoping or unique names.

elaine: @dee good catch. We recently moved some per-model flags into a shared-config overlay to reduce duplication, could have inadvertently changed mount path there.

mike: also check for a k8s provider upgrade in the plan — new provider schema sometimes reorders fields and TF interprets as a change. output of `terraform providers`?

elaine: providers locked at: hashicorp/kubernetes v2.14.0 (no change). I grepped the repo: two files reference /app/config/flags: `overlays/shared-config/kustomization.yaml` and `deploy/helm/models/values.yaml` (the latter via ci render). Looks like CI rendering for the helm chart is now feeding the kustomize overlay with the new path.

sam: sounds like the source of truth mismatch: kustomize overlay vs helm values. two options: 1) revert shared-config change and run a targeted tf plan 2) update TF manifests to accept the new mount path and coordinate rollout. Which is cheaper?

elaine: leaning revert for minimal blast radius. I've opened a short PR to the shared-config overlay to restore /etc/flags and added a regression test in the repo that renders overlays and compares mountPath. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/4122

mike: thanks — can you add a small note to the TF module README about preferred canonical source (kustomize vs helm) so we stop regenerating conflicting manifests?

elaine: good idea, will add. @sam can you review PR 4122 when you have a mo? low risk revert + test.

sam: will review after standup. also add a short CI check to fail when both helm values and kustomize set the same mountPath key to different values — saved me twice. :thumbsup:

elaine: added a basic lint step in the PR pipeline to compare rendered yamls. If it passes, I'll re-run the tf plan and re-apply. infra-bot: please re-run plan once PR is merged.

infra-bot: acknowledged — will queue a targeted plan for k8s_deployment.models-web after PR merge.

dee: moving forward, maybe use a single source of truth for per-model configmount; happy to help draft a short doc.

elaine: thanks everyone, will follow up in the PR with plan output. If Sam signs off I'll merge and re-run apply.

mike: quick FYI — I saw a separate drift yesterday where checksum annotation ordering triggered pod replace; worth checking that our checksum annotation logic sorts keys before hashing.

elaine: noted. I'll add that to the follow-up todo.
